# Combat Systems Analysis

## Case Study 1: Throne & Liberty Build Optimization

### Objective

Investigate the trade\-off between poison\-based gameplay and sustained\-pressure gameplay.

### Hypothesis

Traditional builds may overinvest in poison mechanics at the expense of consistency and accessibility.

### Testing Areas

- Damage Consistency
- Resource Management
- Skill Synergy
- Rotation Complexity
- Build Accessibility

### Key Finding

Players often achieve greater consistency through sustained\-pressure gameplay loops than highly specialized poison\-focused rotations.

### Design Lessons

- Consistency can outperform peak theoretical damage in practical gameplay.
- Resource efficiency frequently influences long\-term performance.
- Build accessibility affects adoption and player satisfaction.
- Players often optimize around reliability rather than maximum output potential.

### Skills Demonstrated

- Combat Design
- Balance Analysis
- Player Decision Making
- Gameplay Flow
- Systems Analysis

